 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "The sign bit (bit 31) comes first. It is 1, so the number is negative. The significand is stored as a magnitude: sign-magnitude, not 2's complement.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "sgn",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       0
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "nsgn",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       0
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Bits 30–23 hold the biased exponent e = 10000001 = 129. Subtracting the bias 127 gives the true exponent E = 2.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "sgn",
     "set": {
      "highlight": []
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "nsgn",
     "set": {
      "highlight": []
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "exp",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       0,
       1,
       2,
       3,
       4,
       5,
       6,
       7
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "nexp",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       0,
       1,
       2,
       3,
       4,
       5,
       6,
       7
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Bits 22–0 hold the fraction f = 1011 followed by zeros. The leading 1 of the significand is hidden, so the significand is 1.1011₂ = 1.6875.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "exp",
     "set": {
      "highlight": []
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "nexp",
     "set": {
      "highlight": []
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "frc",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       0,
       1,
       2,
       3
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "nfr1",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       0,
       1,
       2,
       3
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Put it together: (−1)¹ × 1.1011₂ × 2² = −110.11₂ = −6.75. In hex the word is 0xC0D80000.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "val",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Double precision keeps the same three fields, only wider: 1 sign bit, an 11-bit exponent with bias 1023, and a 52-bit fraction.",
